135.	Nephrotic Syndrome
This condition is associated with proteinuria in excess of 3-3.5 g/1.73 
m2 daily accompanied by hypoalbuminaemia, oedema, hyperlipidaemia 
and hypercoagulable state. Diuretics should be used with caution and not 
given as a routine in children with nephrotic syndrome.
Causes 
yy
Primary Glomerular Disease
yy
Minimal change disease - common in children 
yy
Focal and segmental glomerulosclerosis
yy
Membranous nephropathy
yy
Membranous proliferative glomerulonephritis
yy
Infections
yy
Bacterial (Post streptococcal infection)
yy
Viral-Hepatitis B and C, HIV 
yy
Parasitic (Plasmodium malariae, Schistosoma mansoni, Filaria­
sis)
yy
Systemic Diseases
yy
Diabetes mellitus
yy
Systemic Lupus Erythematosus
yy
Amyloidosis
yy
Drug-related
yy
Non steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs
