141.	Acute Cystitis 
 Acute cystitis is an acute inflammation of the bladder. Women are 
affected 10 times more than men due to the shortness of their urethra 
compared to that of men. 40%-50% of all women will develop cystitis in 
their lifetime. 
The ascending faecal-perineal-urethral route is the primary mode of 
infection. Occasionally sexually transmitted organisms are involved. Risk 
factors include urethral catheterization and diabetes.
