rination (dysuria) yy Lower abdominal pain (bladder pain) Signs yy Pallor yy Palpable kidney from hydronephrosis due to ureteric stricture yy Palpable bladder from bladder cancer or retention of urine due to clots or bladder neck stenosis yy DRE may reveal a fibrosed prostate, enlarged seminal vesicle or thickened bladder base Investigations yy FBC yy Urine for red blood cells, pus cells, and schistosoma ova (mid-day urine specimen preferably taken after physical exercise is ideal) yy Midstream urine for culture in associated urinary tract infections yy Imaging: Ultrasound scan; Intravenous Urogram (IVU) may show','— Urinary Schistosomiasis —
